{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omniintelligence/pulls/817","id":4137699118,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQVCVdc72oEcu","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omniintelligence/pull/817","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omniintelligence/pull/817.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omniintelligence/pull/817.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omniintelligence/issues/817","number":817,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(OMN-15199): slim CLAUDE.md to the proven root pattern (42,089 -> 19,988 bytes)","user":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nCloses OMN-15199 (epic OMN-15197). Slims `omniintelligence/CLAUDE.md` end to end using the proven root-pattern method (omni_home root 64,334 → 30,766; canary OMN-15198 omnibase_infra 43,049 → 18,136, PR omnibase_infra#2482): delete drift-prone state, delete content duplicated from the always-loaded root CLAUDE.md, delete generic advice, replace procedure and illustrative snippets with pointers at real code.\n\n**42,089 → 19,988 bytes** (target was ~24,000; every cut is justified below).\n\nNo GENERATED block exists in this file (verified: no markers, no script in the repo writes CLAUDE.md).\n\n## KEEP contract — live-verified before preservation (8/8 checked, 2 corrected)\n\nEvery KEEP item from the survey was verified against source before being preserved. Two were **live-false** and are corrected, not preserved:\n\n| # | KEEP item | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|-----------|---------|----------|\n| 1 | Fingerprint ordering risk (missing `idempotency_records` at first boot ⇒ poisoned auto-stamp ⇒ later boots fail with `SchemaFingerprintMismatchError`) | **CORRECTED — stale** | `runtime/plugin.py` B1.5 `_check_cross_repo_tables` (OMN-3531) raises `RuntimeHostError` with the provisioning command when the table is absent, *before* B2 runs; the B2 first-boot auto-stamp additionally aborts when live table count < manifest count. The poisoned-fingerprint scenario is defended twice; the migrations-first invariant is kept with the corrected failure mode |\n| 2 | `AdapterPatternStore` ignores `conn`; each method is an independent transaction | TRUE — `repositories/adapter_pattern_store.py` (one-time warning logged, param ignored) | kept |\n| 3 | `wire_dispatchers()` before `start_consumers()` — no dispatch engine = no consumers | TRUE — `start_consumers` returns `skipped` when `_dispatch_engine is None`; also raises if handshake not validated | kept |\n| 4 | Effect nodes never block on Kafka; optional producer, skip/log when absent | TRUE — `producer is not None` guards across effect handlers; contracts declare `required: false` | kept |\n| 5 | 4th protocol for same resource ⇒ refactor existing first | TRUE — protocols verified at `protocols/__init__.py` + node handler modules | kept |\n| 6 | `store_with_version_transition()` for atomic version transitions | TRUE — `adapter_pattern_store.py:564`, declared in `learned_patterns.repository.yaml` | kept |\n| 7 | API module internal-only, no auth, network-topology restricted | TRUE — no auth dependency in `api/`; `Depends` used only for DI | kept |\n| 8 | Hook status: UserPromptSubmit + Stop ACTIVE; SessionStart/SessionEnd/PreToolUse/**PostToolUse** DEFERRED; Notification IGNORED | **CORRECTED — stale** | `handler_claude_event.py` routes `POST_TOOL_USE` and `POST_TOOL_USE_FAILURE` to `handle_post_tool_use()`, which persists to `agent_actions` (OMN-2984) and degrades to no-op when no repository is injected. PostToolUse is ACTIVE, not DEFERRED |\n\n**Additional corrected false claims found during verification:**\n- The \"Enforcement (CI/Audit)\" table cited `tests/audit/test_io_violations.py` for four rules — that file does not exist. Purity is enforced by `tests/unit/test_node_purity.py` (AST purity validator, OMN-1140), whose actual rules differ (interface methods allowed, stub nodes excluded, no line-count check). Corrected.\n- `-m audit` was described as \"I/O purity enforcement (AST checks)\" — `tests/audit/` now contains model-type-safety and pattern-status audits; purity lives under `-m unit`. Corrected.\n- Snippet line counts (~22/~35/~40) were stale (real files: 47/82/103 lines) — moot after replacing snippets with pointers.\n\n## Where each deleted section landed\n\n- 3 illustrative node snippets → pointers to the real exemplar files (`node_quality_scoring_compute/node.py`, `node_claude_hook_event_effect/node.py`, `node_pattern_promotion_effect/node.py`)\n- Contract YAML full example (~2.7KB) → pointer at a real `contract.yaml` + one-paragraph key inventory\n- RuntimeHostProcess boilerplate + anti-pattern table (~4KB) → compressed prose + pointer at `omnibase_infra/src/omnibase_infra/runtime/runtime_host_process.py` (core-owned architecture)\n- \"Key topics\" table + Testing-section subscribe/publish tables + duplicated hook/DLQ/correlation blocks → `docs/reference/EVENT_SURFACE.md` (the file's own stated source of truth; tables were self-contradicting that rule)\n- `EnumIntelligenceOperationType` operations table → pointer at `enums/enum_intelligence_operation_type.py`; FSM flows → `enums/enum_fsm.py`\n- Repository operations table → pointer at `repositories/learned_patterns.repository.yaml`\n- Hardcoded node counts (60/59) → `pyproject.toml [project.entry-points.\"onex.nodes\"]` + `docs/reference/NODE_INVENTORY.md`\n- Handler/protocol/mock code snippets, Key Dependencies table → provably redundant with the source files they quoted (`pyproject.toml`, handler dirs, `tests/conftest.py`)\n- Drift-prone dispatch counts (\"31 handlers / 40 routes\", \"14 modules\") → dropped in favor of `dispatch_handler_*.py` glob description\n\nCompanion doc coherence: `docs/reference/EVENT_SURFACE.md` and `docs/INDEX.md` no longer cite \"CLAUDE.md topic tables\" as a verification source (contract YAML is the single source).\n\n## dod_evidence\n\n- **Bytes**: 42,089 → 19,988 (`wc -c CLAUDE.md` at 6ab20bc7); target ≤ ~24,000 met\n- **KEEP contract**: 8/8 live-verified against source; 2 corrected with file-level evidence (above) per the survey's stale-fact-vector protocol\n- **No new per-repo/per-branch state assertions introduced**; drift-prone facts replaced with the file/command that regenerates them\n- **Gates**: `pre-commit run --files CLAUDE.md docs/INDEX.md docs/reference/EVENT_SURFACE.md` — all hooks Passed/Skipped(no files) on `.200` (Stickybeatz-Studio); docs-only diff, no Python changes\n- **Edit-locality**: edited locally, patch-transferred to `.200`, sha256-verified identical (`c4ba8adc… CLAUDE.md`, `48aa4b7f… docs/INDEX.md`, `2af75ee9… docs/reference/EVENT_SURFACE.md`), committed and pushed from `.200`\n- **Worktree**: `$OMNI_HOME/omni_worktrees/OMN-15199/omniintelligence`, branched from `origin/dev` @ 287f0018 (workspace rule 9 respected)\n\nEvidence-Ticket: OMN-15199\nEvidence-Source: OCC#5012\n","created_at":"2026-07-26T20:33:19Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T20:52:19Z","closed_at":"2026-07-26T20:52:17Z","merged_at":"2026-07-26T20:52:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"f14e18d3